   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Jun 13, 2017 at 8:42 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">youngju...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Group,<div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">I have following questions about removing <span>batch</span> effect by using methylKit (command assocComp and removeComp).</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">1. From the example (<a href=\"https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793231792422000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0JscRD1dI2bKqh-NBsJb7X\">https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf</a>), batch_id and age were used for sampleAnnotation. </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">I wonder can I use sampleAnnotation with only batch_id (or at least two parameter?). </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>yes, you can.</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">2. When I conducted assocComp with 30 samples (15 control, 15 test), I got 30 PCs. </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Is it normal to get the same number of PC as sample?</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>Yes, that is how PCA works. The function tests which PCs are associated with sample annotations</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">3. After I conducted assocComp, I got $pcs, $vars, and $associations. I read explanation of them from here (<a href=\"https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793231792422000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0JscRD1dI2bKqh-NBsJb7X\">https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf</a>).</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">However,  But I did not understand them. More specifically, I did not understand what PC should be deleted based on what ($vars or $association? with what cut-off?).</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>$association  matrix has the P-values that comes from a statistical test for association of PCs with sample annotations. If a PC is significantly associated with batch ids you can try to remove it, this is a crude way of dealing with batch effects.</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;methylkit_discussion&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_discussion+unsub...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_discussion@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793231792422000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-ZEfW2OZFKK2evaqhYMwh\">https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793231792422000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QiBDQok2qKDxUk4Hxp3ca\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
